 "notes": "Headline SK exclusion from Fig.4 (e-print boundsSK_g_vs_ma_8.pdf), the solid-outlined magenta 'Diffuse SN ALP flux (this work)' closed region in the (g_ap, m_a) plane, combining the first four SK phases (dominated by SK-IV). Points trace the full closed contour of the SK region (drawing index 5, solid stroke), NOT the dashed HK projection (drawing 4, out of scope). x converted MeV->eV; y calibrated on log-axis major ticks (10^-7..10^-4). Paper's Lagrangian Eq.1 is L = g_a (d_mu a / 2 m_N)[C_ap p-bar gamma^mu gamma5 p + ...] with g_ap = g_a C_ap, i.e. exactly the canonical L=(g_aN/2m_N)d_mu a N-bar gamma^mu gamma5 N normalisation (2m_N already included); no factor conversion needed. Benchmark model C_ap=-0.47, C_an=0 (g_an=0), KSVZ-inspired. Excluded band spans g_ap ~ 2.5e-5 (lower reach, flat) to ~2.3e-4 (upper 'ceiling' from ALP trapping/reabsorption) over m_a ~ 1-63 MeV (abstract states 1-70 MeV, ~2e-5 to ~2e-4). Not a dark-matter search (diffuse galactic SN flux), so dm_density_assumed=null. 95% C.L. (Z=1.96, profiled log-likelihood ratio, Appendix B).",
